{"delayMs":0,"event":{"seq":3,"runId":"run_a35c8d1f31ff","ts":"2026-07-14T18:32:56.572Z","type":"run.plan_generated","payload":{"plan":[{"index":0,"title":"Inspect existing repo files","detail":"Read Makefile and main.c to understand current build structure, linker script, and any existing stubs. Confirm toolchain and RTT integration approach (the repo ships rtt-f303re.elf/bin which are likely the RTT viewer stub or a pre-built object we link against).","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":1,"title":"Write BMP180 I2C driver in main.c","detail":"Replace/write main.c with a complete register-level I2C1 driver for STM32F303RE at 8 MHz HSI: (1) Enable GPIOB and I2C1 clocks; (2) Configure PB8/PB9 as AF4 open-drain; (3) Set I2C1 TIMINGR for 100 kHz standard mode at 8 MHz (value 0x00201D2B from AN4235); (4) Enable I2C1; (5) Read BMP180 chip-id register 0xD0, assert 0x55; (6) Read 22-byte calibration EEPROM (0xAA\u20130xBF); (7) Trigger uncompensated temperature (OSS=0) and pressure (OSS=0) conversions; (8) Compute true temperature and pressure using BMP180 datasheet algorithm; (9) Output results via RTT (SEGGER_RTT_printf). Loop every 2 s.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":2,"title":"Build firmware","detail":"Run 'make clean && make' and confirm exit code 0 and that rtt-f303re.elf is produced.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":3,"title":"Verify bench hardware is connected","detail":"Call list_targets and list_analyzers to confirm the debug probe and LA2016 are enumerated before any flash/capture attempt.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":4,"title":"Flash firmware to Nucleo-F303RE","detail":"Flash rtt-f303re.elf using pyocd. This is an approval-gated hardware mutation.","riskLevel":"medium","hardwareAction":true},{"index":5,"title":"Capture I2C bus traffic with logic analyzer","detail":"Run capture_during while firmware is running. Configure sigrok with i2c decoder, CH0=SDA, CH1=SCL. Capture ~3 s of traffic covering at least one full chip-id read and one temperature/pressure conversion cycle.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":true},{"index":6,"title":"Read RTT log for sensor output","detail":"Call read_firmware_log to capture RTT output. Expect to see chip-id confirmation (0x55), calibration read confirmation, and printed temperature / pressure values.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":7,"title":"Record all checks and write final report","detail":"Record pass/fail for every registered check (build success, chip-id, I2C ACK, SCL frequency, temperature range, pressure range). Call write_report with evidence-linked Markdown.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false}],"riskSummary":"Two hardware mutations occur in this run. (1) Flash: pyocd overwrites the MCU flash with the new BMP180 firmware \u2014 gated on human approval; a failed flash leaves the board in an unknown state but is recoverable by re-flashing. (2) Logic-analyzer capture: passive tap on SDA/SCL lines \u2014 read-only, zero risk to the board. The board is USB-powered; 3V3 rail is confirmed by the board profile. No erase-only or mass-erase calls are made."}}}
